{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And cast it before Pharaoh — it shall become a tanin</b> — and it does not say 'and it became' (ויהי) but rather: after you cast it, say to the staff, 'become a tanin' — so that Pharaoh will hear that by your word it reverts to a tanin. And why a tanin? Because Pharaoh said of himself: 'the great tanin that lies in your rivers' (Ezekiel 29:3). And He hinted to him: just as this was a tanin and reverted to being dry wood, so will Pharaoh revert to being dust, maggot, and worm."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:07.422882233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}